			<!-- The quest icons (try 4, 2026-10-18): Blizzard's Tab panel type (HeroLeaderPanelTemplate,
			     as Ahli's talents pane) of our own, parked off the screen so nothing of it shows
			     (try 3's sat over the pane and leaked faded portraits), but each row's default-quest
			     icon (BaseQuestIcon0), anchored back onto our row's quest cell by its handle
			     (FCJH_QuestCell0-9). Our talents panel's own quest icons showed Blizzard's shared
			     quest tooltip but never filled it - only a leader panel's icons write into it
			     (docs/blizzard-fixes.md) - so these are a leader panel's, with that shared tooltip.
			     The rows' talents view (TalentsContainerFrame) is the tab Blizzard's TabControl
			     hides; held on as Blizzard's own stats panel holds its stats view on
			     (StatsForceVisible: shown again 0.1 s after the row, or our pane, shows).
			     Blizzard's icon whole (68, the picture 40 at its 14 inset - our cell), so it keeps
			     the quest ring (progress, done) round it (user, 2026-10-16); only its talent border
			     and background are gone, Blizzard's QuestState restated without them.
			     Batch off, as everything we lift (HANDOFF). -->
			<Frame type="HeroLeaderPanel" name="FCJH_QuestPanel" template="HeroLeaderPanel/HeroLeaderPanelTemplate">
